Capstone: Comparative Case Study, Critical Essay, and Visual Argument", "description": "Culminates in a research-based comparison of buildings, cities, or practices using images, maps, drawings, and scholarly argument.", "children": [{"id": "94b8668d-6ce0-437b-8267-7d4da78fd55b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case selection", "children": [{"id": "f8fc44da-ddf0-4c3f-a581-1f2a7be41880", "type": "concept", "title": "Shared theme or typology"}, {"id": "be5fa465-7665-49e0-9afc-be4431180d81", "type": "concept", "title": "Different regions or political contexts"}, {"id": "2dc4e0af-a115-4512-a545-656b8e93a9d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Clear archive and evidence base"}], "description": "Students learn to choose cases that produce a meaningful comparison rather than a list of examples."}, {"id": "676d8250-ce34-4740-b488-48353f9cbe5b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visual argument", "children": [{"id": "04eaefac-5a3a-42a1-81ea-24a744f80dee", "type": "concept", "title": "Annotated drawings"}, {"id": "016ca7b5-06d9-47c8-8283-6d1d8e0dfe33", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparative timelines"}, {"id": "2eaab0b3-d435-4643-95f1-66e2a5c3795a", "type": "concept", "title": "Mapping networks and flows"}], "description": "The capstone requires images, maps, and diagrams to carry historical claims."}, {"id": "156eacd0-370a-42c5-8759-88b9086bcd47", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research writing", "children": [{"id": "bc60a366-2e49-4450-9e31-7da72386976b", "type": "concept", "title": "Thesis and stakes"}, {"id": "d2655f52-5412-4ebc-9d33-ed79c4e64f2a", "type": "concept", "title": "Source integration"}, {"id": "470ebbcf-33e6-497a-9a80-cf4cfef70082", "type": "concept", "title": "Revision, captions, and bibliography"}], "description": "Students convert analysis into a polished scholarly argument."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$ahi3json$::jsonb,
